igging to figure out how  it would be possible and there's a few  ways where you can connect it to your  computer with a cable and use the photos  app but the simplest one I found is to  export your image to the files app let  it upload if it's your iCloud drive and  then select the image and then share it  and move it back to your photo roll and  then go back to photos find the raw and  then delete it and even then that only  works if you edited the image if you  didn't then it will transfer the  original huge file and if you did edit  the image but then you want to transfer  the full resolution to edit well you  can't do that you have to undo all the  edits first and then you can transfer it  this is crazy there should be a pop-up  that asks you which version you want to  export and also an option to convert to  JPEG and automatically delete the raw as  of now apple is just telling people that  the pro raw files take up a lot of space  and you will run out of room and you  should upgrade your storage if you have  iCloud go get the new plan and there's  even a link there to help you to spend  more money alright I gotta calm down a  little bit and just say that after all  this real world use and testing overall  I am very happy mainly due to the  reception and the speed improvements as  well as the convenience of the always-on  display that I wanted for a long time  and the huge speaker boost for me this  is a good upgrade from the 13 Pro and I  would not regret it even if I did not  have this channel so if you guys are  ready for an upgrade you're looking at  the 14 pro I think you'll be very happy  so there you guys go go ahead and click  that subscribe button above if you guys  want to see my super detailed ultimate  camera comparison check out one of those  videos right there this Max and I'll see  you in the next video  [Music]

